#!/usr/bin/env python3
# =============================================================================
# h96-backup-gui - graphical front end for h96-backup and h96-restore.
#
# Pick what to back up (or what to restore from an archive) with checkboxes;
# the tool builds the matching h96-backup / h96-restore command line and runs
# it in a terminal window, so the CLIs' own prompts stay visible. All logic
# lives in the CLIs; this file only selects and launches.
#
#   h96-backup-gui                    open the window
#   h96-backup-gui --restore          open on the Restore tab, newest archive loaded
#   h96-backup-gui --install-desktop  write the application menu entry (root)
#   h96-backup-gui --selftest         print the command lines it would build
#
# Every panel the window draws is its own themed widget. Tk's built-in message
# and file dialogs are not used: they ignore the theme and paint white. Reading
# the box and reading an archive run on a worker thread, so the window keeps
# painting while they work and no unpainted area is left behind.
#
# The Archive and Save-to fields accept a typed path as well as a pick from the
# list: give a file to use it, or a folder to search it for archives.
#
# Needs python3-tk; the first launch installs it through a terminal (apt).
# =============================================================================
